  "tagline": "A Rust stream processor with SQL pipelines, now owned by Cloudflare and powering Cloudflare Pipelines.",
  "description": "Arroyo is a distributed stream-processing engine written in Rust on Apache Arrow and DataFusion, where pipelines are defined in SQL with windows, joins and UDFs, and state is checkpointed to object storage. It aims to be a lighter, cloud-native alternative to Flink. Cloudflare acquired Arroyo Systems in April 2025 and uses it as the transformation engine of Cloudflare Pipelines, which streams data into R2 and Iceberg tables. The engine remains Apache 2.0 and self-hostable; release cadence has slowed since (0.15.0 in December 2025).",
